{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "restriction-enzymes",
  "title": "Type II restriction endonucleases",
  "description": "Recognition sequences and cut positions for commonly used type II restriction endonucleases in the suppliers' and REBASE catalogue notation. topCut is the number of bases between the 5' end of the recognition sequence and the phosphodiester bond cut on the top strand; bottomCut is the same distance, measured in top-strand coordinates, for the cut on the bottom strand. So EcoRI G^AATTC / CTTAA^G is topCut 1, bottomCut 5, and the overhang is bottomCut - topCut: positive for a 5' overhang, negative for a 3' overhang, zero for a blunt cut. Every entry has a palindromic recognition sequence and a cut symmetric about the site centre, which the loader asserts; enzymes that cut asymmetrically outside their recognition sequence are deliberately absent rather than approximated.",
